<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teriimaevarua III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1871">1871</a>–<a href="/years/1932">1932</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teriimaevarua III (1871–1932) was the last queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bora-bora">Bora Bora</a> in the Society Islands, succeeding as a child in 1873 and reigning until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed the island, a process completed in 1895. Her reign saw growing French influence across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leeward Islands</a> after the annexation of Tahiti in 1880.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teriimaevarua-iii.jpg" alt="Teriimaevarua III" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Terii_Maeva_Rua,_Queen_of_Bora_Bora.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
